  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two iron cubes <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"B\"></span> have side lengths <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2L\"></span> respectively. When a temperature difference is placed across two opposite faces of cube <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span>, the power transferred across the cube is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span>. When the same temperature difference is placed across two opposite faces of cube <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"B\"></span>, what is the power transferred across the cube in terms of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span>?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{P}2\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2P\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4P\"></span></p></li></ol>"
